{# gap_fill.j2 — Suggest how a candidate can address skill gaps for a target role.
   Expected context keys:
     missing_skills   (list[str]) — skills/requirements from the JD not found in the resume
     profile_summary  (str)       — candidate's current professional summary
     experience_titles (list[str]) — list of the candidate's past job titles
     job_title        (str)       — target role title
     job_company      (str)       — target company name
     tone             (str)       — desired tone: "professional" | "technical" | "creative"
#}
You are a professional career coach and resume strategist.

A candidate is applying for: {{ job_title }} at {{ job_company }}

Candidate background:
{{ profile_summary }}

Past roles: {{ experience_titles | join(', ') }}

The following required skills or qualifications appear to be missing or under-represented in the candidate's resume:
{% for skill in missing_skills %}
- {{ skill }}
{% endfor %}

For each missing skill, suggest ONE concrete, actionable way the candidate can:
1. Highlight existing (possibly hidden) experience that covers this gap, OR
2. Frame existing skills as transferable, OR
3. Recommend a specific short-term action to close the gap (certification, project, etc.)

Format your response as:

SKILL: [skill name]
SUGGESTION: [one concrete suggestion in 1-2 sentences]

Repeat for each skill. Output ONLY the structured suggestions above, {{ tone }} tone, no extra commentary:
